    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"WORK"</data>
      <data key="d1">NR (Norma Regulamentadora) is a Brazilian normative document that establishes general guidelines and rules for occupational health and safety. It provides comprehensive regulations covering various specific contexts, including electrical installations and the construction industry, with particular provisions addressing safety standards for construction site elevators.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76289beed8234f6f04cc1ad70f9749ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-589cdcf81c05ee920949a7fd05f6584a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45a31aec243f9221915b0830e8138712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38329ca5bd7388723ab2479ab41baab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f3fe8f8bfb9a820642da6555684412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcad9f8ab5b70f8cb31dc94989c157e8</data>
      <data key="d3">56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">The Diário Oficial da União (DOU) is the official Brazilian publication where normative texts are officially published and disseminated. It serves as the primary legal reference for these documents, possessing inherent legal validity. While specific versions of normative texts may be provided for convenience, they are considered non-substitutive references; the DOU remains the authoritative source for the original publication and official legal standing of such regulations.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-687e9c1f3bf6943b349873b3fee88905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c5cf633496698b9fddf89aa606b22a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a87a3f81bc41b911db4b5e5d5f0dcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc556663e5d61db34218f36477303b44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1afdc59c2d3726d04360a596f2f00fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f147b6a0c9b5cced56b4f6a670faf21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861e9f7632d4dfd81c4b7f8a9c0fdea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652dcb3de9fd12345bdfd7125d0dd45f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59befa38d15567b8d7bcc3b001ac5bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-749c2d920844c1bc2154c445fae4f3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f3fe8f8bfb9a820642da6555684412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df2326a15cc9705c8dbcd431d7762be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b99f0e5d971ab8826e3f8221d2258b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcad9f8ab5b70f8cb31dc94989c157e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c698fd9dbd4746b8c175f22d62ca2788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad39a2fc22a6c8914aa4ba8440ccca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f6aac9b4d8e9449b9eed627c3cd47ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ba2773d9f660536f70f2b3fcd5161e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c918d4217cdb86ef20b49d6b6635688e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-589cdcf81c05ee920949a7fd05f6584a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af302f9355e316c7b9d518b53d5e0e38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777529d0ca6ad0353d174f0c0945acab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eac10d0f56e304067eea1b96ec59c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73989acf24197e9db670e73a0b363e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8256f00c2800357558f3e2c0d46b5d01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5936a71a74343d6130e3c767256974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbf99e538c6200c878721962d99f90a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e51e28fc0a2770c84fabe25016e37fdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-461b0578830e92eea6081cabfa2c7404&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d76a42d252722ee5987d1c03002e78b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a4297618074b93c8abbfea3ab8bc40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20876814c61294bf395d2f121a24bddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e39a70a36c8f0f96a14271e365cd6351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75a6634b9377c3127262a76a0c6068e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55d1bf9243ba1aec47c5b4073afe46ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7be1a396d630b24f28daad35f3ca0c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc56add9155f3804c44e96aaffd8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9507a58112032a1366818361a0ca02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ef538556a551b7484cd4f959f104da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780e0f65c9bb24868086ccd3f8d592e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53e002d3295871a52b86e59f30957b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78eb47370c28394e2312174786e0f715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ba30f0a53c36f36a6dd512887c3a223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecd2c1678f36a70efbc2052e1f21985f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cf6f4889c3248de07b4fa8be118ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8cfec1e4a84598830f42efa05e35e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92e21457b35465a6acda0c0787835f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f32ce9b667080358bbbd444693b20180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1210959aca2e55706f5f576974cfb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81eec1f6ee4405401ff40539cf37d1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3502cb66477505db0e22df45c318467</data>
      <data key="d3">85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NR-10&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"WORK"</data>
      <data key="d1">NR-10 is a Brazilian Regulatory Standard (Norma Regulamentadora) that establishes guidelines and minimum measures for implementing safety and health actions in electrical installations and services. Its primary objective is to prevent accidents by ensuring worker safety during the execution of electrical work, including providing specific instructions for employees and protection against associated risks. Additionally, NR-10 serves as a key reference for determining required safety distances in such environments.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfef4b60bf1e84cf5b5d75e4228a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb1e0c16652291b0fd4eb8fdca5edb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4b71ea67c36ef3df5936b68fe06b1be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cf6f4889c3248de07b4fa8be118ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47da6ea501f7dcd04f239daeda449a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf03e00efd6f11dd13601a203c4c955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db29ce757dabf3f7cfeb504155acd7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-795b95f0776946f73846af01f10fc45c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27bda215a442c90cb021c21b98db115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c6e460c3d4f5d08be83abfcf6670e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-461b0578830e92eea6081cabfa2c7404</data>
      <data key="d3">83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NR-12&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">NR-12 is a Brazilian Regulatory Standard (Norma Regulamentadora) that establishes comprehensive guidelines for occupational safety and health specifically regarding machines and equipment. It serves as the fundamental legal basis for defining safety requirements in industrial settings, covering a wide range of protections including those against falls and specific operational conditions for lifting equipment. By setting these standards, NR-12 ensures that workplaces involving machinery adhere to strict safety protocols to protect workers.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-80ef69391dd4e50ae486de13fe53bc42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20876814c61294bf395d2f121a24bddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de72701d9a6338255c6594fcfabb4d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e39a70a36c8f0f96a14271e365cd6351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75a6634b9377c3127262a76a0c6068e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc56add9155f3804c44e96aaffd8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ef538556a551b7484cd4f959f104da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f7df212717dd8ee2d97d84f42a97ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c19301d113ec019bab895c6c2e358ef</data>
      <data key="d3">86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NR-35&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KEYWORD"</data>
      <data key="d1">NR-35 is a Brazilian Regulatory Standard (Norma Regulamentadora) specifically dedicated to work at heights. It establishes guidelines, minimum criteria, and mandatory requirements to ensure the safe execution of such activities. The standard defines the necessary conditions for safety and serves as the foundational basis for the specific training and qualification of workers engaged in high-altitude tasks, including manual excavation of caissons and services performed on roofs that exceed certain height thresholds.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b27bda215a442c90cb021c21b98db115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73989acf24197e9db670e73a0b363e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a1c54fa015a3b79516f9bc8346ed85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9507a58112032a1366818361a0ca02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df2326a15cc9705c8dbcd431d7762be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad39a2fc22a6c8914aa4ba8440ccca4</data>
      <data key="d3">89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NR-18&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"WORK"</data>
      <data key="d1">NR-18, known as Norma Regulamentadora 18, is a Brazilian regulatory standard that establishes the guidelines, conditions, and minimum criteria for promoting safety and health in the construction industry. It specifically addresses work environment conditions within this sector and defines the safety rules and measures required for compliance. The standard is frequently referenced implicitly in relevant texts through the phrase "desta NR," indicating its foundational role in governing occupational safety protocols for construction activities.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1cac7a88894996eee964f97e7f53b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eac10d0f56e304067eea1b96ec59c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8cfec1e4a84598830f42efa05e35e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861e9f7632d4dfd81c4b7f8a9c0fdea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e1b9270c90be9a20387a75f53f5f38a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0493e5a610c1e30af5c60f7524c9e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbf99e538c6200c878721962d99f90a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9507a58112032a1366818361a0ca02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea78fb35e1fd216f5630ffebbc33a65</data>
      <data key="d3">90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORMAS TÉCNICAS NACIONAIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">The NORMAS TÉCNICAS NACIONAIS (National Technical Standards) constitute a comprehensive set of Brazilian regulations and technical standards that define the mandatory requirements for safety, quality, and execution across various industries and processes. These standards govern the specification, installation, and operation of diverse equipment and materials, including gas hoses, cable-traction elevators, steel and synthetic fiber cables, and waterproofing services. By establishing these prevailing rules, the NORMAS TÉCNICAS NACIONAIS ensure that all relevant equipment and processes meet strict national criteria for security, reliability, and traceability.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-020c713238c5b6f009cdf20567f7c222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777529d0ca6ad0353d174f0c0945acab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f147b6a0c9b5cced56b4f6a670faf21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861e9f7632d4dfd81c4b7f8a9c0fdea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-749c2d920844c1bc2154c445fae4f3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9507a58112032a1366818361a0ca02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f7df212717dd8ee2d97d84f42a97ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ba30f0a53c36f36a6dd512887c3a223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcad9f8ab5b70f8cb31dc94989c157e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad39a2fc22a6c8914aa4ba8440ccca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5770fce142de2aa36dc6046f4d477f74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fcca385fcdfc2bf69eb2e54c234a970</data>
      <data key="d3">122</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDÚSTRIA DA CONSTRUÇÃO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">The "INDÚSTRIA DA CONSTRUÇÃO" (Construction Industry) is the specific economic sector to which various regulatory norms, safety standards, and training rules apply. This sector encompasses a broad range of activities, including construction, demolition, repair, painting, cleaning, and maintenance, as well as building (edificação), infrastructure development, and general works. Within this industry, established regulations govern safety, hygiene, health, organization, and protection measures, while also defining the requirements for worker qualification, including specific rules regarding training hours and periodicity.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e4f962ddfced8cca5c2aff7369a661b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1cac7a88894996eee964f97e7f53b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-589cdcf81c05ee920949a7fd05f6584a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27bda215a442c90cb021c21b98db115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861e9f7632d4dfd81c4b7f8a9c0fdea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0493e5a610c1e30af5c60f7524c9e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780e0f65c9bb24868086ccd3f8d592e</data>
      <data key="d3">110</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">APR (Análise Preliminar de Risco) is a safety management tool and procedure utilized to identify hazards prior to execution and determine necessary control measures. It serves as a critical safety document that establishes exposure limits and criteria for releasing areas after services are completed. The APR is required when deemed necessary by Occupational Safety protocols, specifically in situations where there is a technical unfeasibility in using an EPC (Environmental Permit). As such, it outlines alternative safety measures, defines the scope of coverage, specifies signaling requirements, and evaluates overall safety needs to ensure risk mitigation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8256f00c2800357558f3e2c0d46b5d01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a87a3f81bc41b911db4b5e5d5f0dcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59befa38d15567b8d7bcc3b001ac5bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a1c54fa015a3b79516f9bc8346ed85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28f3dbec47aed130afea6282dbc514ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1210959aca2e55706f5f576974cfb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-358ec7fd8808062e3b71ff358982a180</data>
      <data key="d3">115</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRABALHADORES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">TRABALHADORES refers to individuals engaged in various professional activities, including construction services, electrical installations, operations aboard floating structures, and exposure to hyperbaric pressures. These individuals are subject to comprehensive regulatory frameworks designed to preserve their safety and health. Consequently, TRABALHADORES must undergo specific training and possess required medical examinations, particularly those exposed to hyperbaric conditions or working with electrical systems. They are obligated to strictly adhere to established protocols regarding safety, hygiene, and nutrition, ensuring that all preventive measures outlined in relevant norms are followed to protect their well-being in their respective work environments.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76289beed8234f6f04cc1ad70f9749ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1cac7a88894996eee964f97e7f53b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c918d4217cdb86ef20b49d6b6635688e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eac10d0f56e304067eea1b96ec59c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4b71ea67c36ef3df5936b68fe06b1be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45a31aec243f9221915b0830e8138712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27bda215a442c90cb021c21b98db115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f147b6a0c9b5cced56b4f6a670faf21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db29ce757dabf3f7cfeb504155acd7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbd1178d5247813c887400ec4a07304b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9507a58112032a1366818361a0ca02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f32ce9b667080358bbbd444693b20180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b99f0e5d971ab8826e3f8221d2258b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780e0f65c9bb24868086ccd3f8d592e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fcca385fcdfc2bf69eb2e54c234a970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-461b0578830e92eea6081cabfa2c7404</data>
      <data key="d3">124</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANDAIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARTIFICIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">ANDAIME is a temporary structure utilized in construction sites primarily as a work platform to provide access to elevated areas and to support both workers and materials. Typically composed of vertical elements such as standards (montantes) and other structural components, it serves as a critical means of working at height. The design, fabrication, assembly, disassembly, and dimensional sizing of an ANDAIME are subject to rigorous technical standards and specific safety regulations that ensure its stability and integrity. Consequently, the structure requires strict adherence to maintenance protocols and must undergo formal verification and official release regarding safety compliance before being authorized for use.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e73989acf24197e9db670e73a0b363e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-749c2d920844c1bc2154c445fae4f3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38329ca5bd7388723ab2479ab41baab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5936a71a74343d6130e3c767256974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c698fd9dbd4746b8c175f22d62ca2788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31723b05ed7f3abc65c5959c61472c4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53e002d3295871a52b86e59f30957b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ba30f0a53c36f36a6dd512887c3a223</data>
      <data key="d3">120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CABOS DE AÇO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARTIFICIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">CABOS DE AÇO (steel cables) are robust metallic structural components primarily utilized as tension elements in lifting systems and for the movement of heavy loads. They serve critical functions in various industrial applications, including use in suspended chairs, load support structures, and as rigid safety devices connected to anchorage points. To ensure operational integrity and prevent accidental escape, these cables are subject to containment or fixation devices at pulleys and require rigorous inspection by signalmen. As essential equipment for safety and support, CABOS DE AÇO must meet specific standards to guarantee their reliability in sustaining heavy weights and maintaining structural stability.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-687e9c1f3bf6943b349873b3fee88905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eac10d0f56e304067eea1b96ec59c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a87a3f81bc41b911db4b5e5d5f0dcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55d1bf9243ba1aec47c5b4073afe46ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-749c2d920844c1bc2154c445fae4f3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5eb5f66be2a7e8a5a4b2869f3ba61e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad39a2fc22a6c8914aa4ba8440ccca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53e002d3295871a52b86e59f30957b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ef69391dd4e50ae486de13fe53bc42</data>
      <data key="d3">122</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORTARIA MTB Nº 836&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"WORK"</data>
      <data key="d1">PORTARIA MTB Nº 836 is a normative document issued by the Ministry of Labor on October 9, 2018, which introduced several amendments to existing regulations. Specifically, this ordinance inserted the definition of Maritime Authority into the regulatory text and included provisions regarding services supported by floating structures. Additionally, it modified the rules concerning work in adverse weather conditions, particularly adjusting wind speed limits, and incorporated dispositions related to the PRE (Professional Risk Evaluation). Finally, PORTARIA MTB Nº 836 renumbered the final provisions of the relevant legislation to ensure coherence within the updated text.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-777529d0ca6ad0353d174f0c0945acab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59befa38d15567b8d7bcc3b001ac5bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652dcb3de9fd12345bdfd7125d0dd45f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0deed7b26b545e1877e03ce39a97254d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71c8ca74b83532683a7a57904153edda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5936a71a74343d6130e3c767256974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a15d5cb124a27cf65c36311d46e61c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31723b05ed7f3abc65c5959c61472c4a</data>
      <data key="d3">122</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NR-34&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">NR-34 is a Brazilian Regulatory Standard (Norma Regulamentadora) that establishes guidelines and minimum criteria for planning and managing occupational safety and health. It specifically applies to operations involving the construction, assembly, manufacturing, maintenance, and dismantling of metal structures. The standard covers a range of high-risk activities, including work at heights—such as lifting operations and scaffold assembly—as well as work in confined spaces and hot work activities. These specific aspects are detailed within the regulation, with references to hot work and confined space protocols appearing in sections such as item 34.14 and associated training materials.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1b9ab0eb29b76caf7836ed396330ed8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b99f0e5d971ab8826e3f8221d2258b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5eb5f66be2a7e8a5a4b2869f3ba61e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c698fd9dbd4746b8c175f22d62ca2788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1210959aca2e55706f5f576974cfb6</data>
      <data key="d3">120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIQ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">SPIQ, which stands for Sistema de Proteção Individual Contra Quedas (Individual Fall Protection System), is a mandatory piece of personal protective equipment required during assembly and disassembly operations to mitigate the risk of falls. It is specifically mandated for all horizontal and vertical access points where there is a potential hazard of falling. This includes mandatory usage on fixed vertical ladders with a height exceeding two meters and for vertical access to command cabins when necessary. Additionally, SPIQ systems are essential for roof access, which must be designed to prevent fall risks. The system utilizes synthetic fiber cables as vertical lifelines to ensure worker safety in these elevated environments.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e4f962ddfced8cca5c2aff7369a661b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eac10d0f56e304067eea1b96ec59c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de72701d9a6338255c6594fcfabb4d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73989acf24197e9db670e73a0b363e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f147b6a0c9b5cced56b4f6a670faf21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc56add9155f3804c44e96aaffd8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e1b9270c90be9a20387a75f53f5f38a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38329ca5bd7388723ab2479ab41baab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbf99e538c6200c878721962d99f90a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9507a58112032a1366818361a0ca02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f3fe8f8bfb9a820642da6555684412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-749c2d920844c1bc2154c445fae4f3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ba30f0a53c36f36a6dd512887c3a223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ef69391dd4e50ae486de13fe53bc42</data>
      <data key="d3">128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANÁLISE DE RISCO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">ANÁLISE DE RISCO is a mandatory risk management process and safety evaluation tool utilized across various operational contexts to assess hazards and determine safety conditions. It serves as a required step in specific procedures for authorizing work under particular conditions, such as strong winds or proximity to electrical grids, and is essential for evaluating risks associated with hot work, particularly in areas containing flammable materials or lacking prior isolation. Additionally, ANÁLISE DE RISCO is applied to analyze dangers linked to material handling, including both routine and non-routine load movements and lifting operations, as well as before the implementation of technological innovations or the commissioning of new electrical equipment.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3eac10d0f56e304067eea1b96ec59c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-589cdcf81c05ee920949a7fd05f6584a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de72701d9a6338255c6594fcfabb4d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777529d0ca6ad0353d174f0c0945acab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf03e00efd6f11dd13601a203c4c955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db29ce757dabf3f7cfeb504155acd7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652dcb3de9fd12345bdfd7125d0dd45f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f3fe8f8bfb9a820642da6555684412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ef538556a551b7484cd4f959f104da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea78fb35e1fd216f5630ffebbc33a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c6e460c3d4f5d08be83abfcf6670e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad39a2fc22a6c8914aa4ba8440ccca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81eec1f6ee4405401ff40539cf37d1e6</data>
      <data key="d3">130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORTARIA MTE Nº 836&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">PORTARIA MTE Nº 836 is a normative administrative act issued by the Ministry of Labor and Employment (Ministério do Trabalho e Emprego) on May 13, 2026. This regulation serves as the most recent listed update to existing standards, altering the wording of specific items within the norm. Its primary focus is the insertion of new requirements regarding safety measures against falling materials in construction sites, specifically introducing new stipulations and definitions for multidirectional scaffolds (Andaime Multidirecional). The portaria establishes these updated provisions with an effective date of June 29, 2026.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0493e5a610c1e30af5c60f7524c9e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8cfec1e4a84598830f42efa05e35e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-749c2d920844c1bc2154c445fae4f3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38329ca5bd7388723ab2479ab41baab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbf99e538c6200c878721962d99f90a3</data>
      <data key="d3">129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRABALHOS A QUENTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">**TRABALHOS A QUENTE** refers to industrial and maintenance operations that involve the generation of heat, sparks, or flames, such as welding and cutting processes. These activities are subject to specific safety regulations and require strict protocols, including prior inspection of the work area and the sealing of openings to mitigate risks. To ensure safety, specific precautions are mandated during these operations: the use of wooden ladders is strictly prohibited due to fire hazards, and the wearing of contact lenses is forbidden due to the presence of high temperatures and open flames. Consequently, **TRABALHOS A QUENTE** necessitate continuous monitoring and adherence to rigorous safety standards to prevent accidents.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6a4297618074b93c8abbfea3ab8bc40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59befa38d15567b8d7bcc3b001ac5bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a1c54fa015a3b79516f9bc8346ed85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0deed7b26b545e1877e03ce39a97254d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71c8ca74b83532683a7a57904153edda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5eb5f66be2a7e8a5a4b2869f3ba61e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5770fce142de2aa36dc6046f4d477f74</data>
      <data key="d3">135</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RODAPÉ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARTIFICIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">The RODAPÉ (toe board) is a mandatory safety barrier installed at the base of scaffolds, ladders, ramps, walkways, and work platforms. It functions as a horizontal component with a minimum height of 0.15 meters (15 cm) or 20 cm, depending on specific regulatory contexts, positioned flush against the working surface or along the bottom edge of guardrails. This barrier is required when the floor level is above 1.00 meter and serves as part of the overall protection system to prevent the falling of tools, materials, or objects, as well as to impede the passage of people through the edges of the platform.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07c5cf633496698b9fddf89aa606b22a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75a6634b9377c3127262a76a0c6068e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59befa38d15567b8d7bcc3b001ac5bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8cfec1e4a84598830f42efa05e35e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38329ca5bd7388723ab2479ab41baab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbf99e538c6200c878721962d99f90a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c698fd9dbd4746b8c175f22d62ca2788</data>
      <data key="d3">134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESPONSÁVEL TÉCNICO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">The RESPONSÁVEL TÉCNICO is a legally qualified professional formally designated by the employer to oversee critical technical and safety aspects within the organization. This individual is responsible for establishing the planning and schedule for simulated emergency exercises, as well as classifying structural elements and developing, issuing, and revising both general and specific procedures for safety and fixation. Additionally, the RESPONSÁVEL TÉCNICO is identified in the PRE (Plano de Resgate de Emergência) as the authority responsible for elaborating and reviewing the plan, approving preventive maintenance programs, and ensuring the implementation of safety procedures. A key duty involves signing the Equipment Logbook (Prontuário dos Equipamentos) to guarantee compliance with established safety protocols.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3ba2773d9f660536f70f2b3fcd5161e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777529d0ca6ad0353d174f0c0945acab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652dcb3de9fd12345bdfd7125d0dd45f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28f3dbec47aed130afea6282dbc514ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71c8ca74b83532683a7a57904153edda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92e21457b35465a6acda0c0787835f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78eb47370c28394e2312174786e0f715</data>
      <data key="d3">146</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRABALHADOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">The TRABALHADOR is an individual who performs various labor activities, including work at heights, rope access operations, construction, assembly, maintenance tasks, and the use of portable ladders. To ensure safety and compliance, the TRABALHADOR must adhere to established security norms and protocols, such as maintaining three points of support when using portable ladders and connecting to anchor points during rope access activities. Additionally, the TRABALHADOR requires specific training and certification for height-related work and is mandated to use both personal and collective protective equipment. As a subject exposed to occupational risks, such as falls and other workplace hazards, the TRABALHADOR is the primary target of the comfort and safety measures described in the relevant regulatory texts.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-687e9c1f3bf6943b349873b3fee88905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d76a42d252722ee5987d1c03002e78b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-020c713238c5b6f009cdf20567f7c222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5936a71a74343d6130e3c767256974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71c8ca74b83532683a7a57904153edda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f3fe8f8bfb9a820642da6555684412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0110767f6db591ee0b38d305f6ff2756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff7ee508bd72306907acf96114dabee0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ba30f0a53c36f36a6dd512887c3a223</data>
      <data key="d3">150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMPRESA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">EMPRESA is defined as an organized economic unit and legal entity that serves as the contracting or operating organization within a project. As the employer, EMPRESA is responsible for designating technical managers, implementing safety procedures, and establishing systems for identification and authorization. It holds the authority to grant third-party access to the project and is obligated to maintain relevant documentation up to date. Furthermore, EMPRESA must ensure strict compliance with safety standards and workforce training requirements. In terms of occupational health and safety, EMPRESA is required to adopt preventive and corrective measures following accidents, provide necessary rescue means, and legally mandate the development, implementation, and continuous updating of Emergency Response Plans. Additionally, EMPRESA guarantees that workers on board receive free access to quality food and specific dietary accommodations.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c918d4217cdb86ef20b49d6b6635688e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777529d0ca6ad0353d174f0c0945acab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73989acf24197e9db670e73a0b363e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-795b95f0776946f73846af01f10fc45c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8035da2289e8087164d9a280d2a5d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28f3dbec47aed130afea6282dbc514ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8335d33c4efb992b42a42fa3597b5c</data>
      <data key="d3">156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPERADOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">The OPERADOR is a professional individual responsible for the daily operation, conduct, and management of various equipment, including load-handling machinery, Personal Material Transport Equipment (PEMT), and elevators. Their core duties encompass operating the machinery while adhering to strict safety protocols, such as maintaining clear visibility of load tables and obstacles, keeping a safe distance from hazards, limiting displacement speed, and following the instructions of a signalman, unless there is imminent risk. Beyond driving, the OPERADOR is tasked with routine maintenance and organization, which includes cleaning the equipment, organizing loads, separating people from materials, and reporting any anomalies. Additionally, when operating specific machines, the OPERADOR is protected by a hood against potential risks and is authorized to perform transport operations.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76289beed8234f6f04cc1ad70f9749ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20876814c61294bf395d2f121a24bddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cf6f4889c3248de07b4fa8be118ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a87a3f81bc41b911db4b5e5d5f0dcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f147b6a0c9b5cced56b4f6a670faf21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0deed7b26b545e1877e03ce39a97254d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f7df212717dd8ee2d97d84f42a97ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c698fd9dbd4746b8c175f22d62ca2788</data>
      <data key="d3">150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EQUIPAMENTO DE GUINDAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARTIFICIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">EQUIPAMENTO DE GUINDAR refers to a category of equipment and primary machinery designed for the vertical transportation, lifting, and movement of materials and heavy loads. This classification includes specific devices such as cranes, winches, and hoists, which function as mechanisms whose operational capacity varies depending on their configuration. The equipment is utilized not only for general load handling but also for the fixation and stabilization of structural elements. Operationally, EQUIPAMENTO DE GUINDAR is subject to strict regulatory frameworks, requiring adherence to specific safety norms, routine inspections, and official certifications. Furthermore, its deployment and release often depend on formal authorization from the Responsible Person (RO), and certain configurations may require additional stabilization measures, such as ballasting, to ensure safe operation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-687e9c1f3bf6943b349873b3fee88905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8256f00c2800357558f3e2c0d46b5d01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a87a3f81bc41b911db4b5e5d5f0dcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c19301d113ec019bab895c6c2e358ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652dcb3de9fd12345bdfd7125d0dd45f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0deed7b26b545e1877e03ce39a97254d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5936a71a74343d6130e3c767256974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea78fb35e1fd216f5630ffebbc33a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5eb5f66be2a7e8a5a4b2869f3ba61e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53e002d3295871a52b86e59f30957b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ef69391dd4e50ae486de13fe53bc42</data>
      <data key="d3">154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMPREGADOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">The EMPREGADOR (Employer) is the contracting party and organizational entity responsible for hiring, managing workers, and formally designating legally qualified professionals for technical responsibility. As a key stakeholder, the EMPREGADOR holds legal obligations to ensure safe working conditions, which includes providing up-to-date information on risks, interrupting dangerous activities when necessary, and taking measures to eliminate hazards, such as installing physical protections against fire and splashes. Additionally, the EMPREGADOR is tasked with overseeing worker training and development by defining the content and workload of both periodic and occasional trainings, ensuring that safety standards are compatible with the specific activities involved. This role also extends to authorizing the waiver of internships and assuming full responsibility for the professional's capacity building and overall training compliance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-58fd45d2ee14671afd511b654fd72573&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e39a70a36c8f0f96a14271e365cd6351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-020c713238c5b6f009cdf20567f7c222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73989acf24197e9db670e73a0b363e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1b9ab0eb29b76caf7836ed396330ed8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc56add9155f3804c44e96aaffd8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652dcb3de9fd12345bdfd7125d0dd45f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71c8ca74b83532683a7a57904153edda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ef538556a551b7484cd4f959f104da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f32ce9b667080358bbbd444693b20180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b99f0e5d971ab8826e3f8221d2258b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780e0f65c9bb24868086ccd3f8d592e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad39a2fc22a6c8914aa4ba8440ccca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea22aefdc64a322b6e5679d34d0f8bb</data>
      <data key="d3">154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRABALHADOR CAPACITADO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">The "TRABALHADOR CAPACITADO" (Qualified Worker) is an individual who possesses the necessary qualifications and training, often in accordance with specific normative requirements such as Annex I, to perform specialized tasks safely. This role encompasses a wide range of authorized activities, including the operation, installation, and maintenance of work platforms and lifting equipment, as well as the operation of portable rotating equipment. Additionally, a "TRABALHADOR CAPACITADO" is qualified to execute hot work activities with safety protocols and is required to guide operators of self-propelled machinery when their visibility is compromised. The qualification process for this worker involves receiving training under the guidance and responsibility of a legally enabled and authorized professional, typically working under the same supervision to ensure compliance with safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20876814c61294bf395d2f121a24bddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73989acf24197e9db670e73a0b363e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc556663e5d61db34218f36477303b44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8035da2289e8087164d9a280d2a5d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea22aefdc64a322b6e5679d34d0f8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28f3dbec47aed130afea6282dbc514ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc9d148efe9a2559b7beaa15d4eb102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a15d5cb124a27cf65c36311d46e61c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f32ce9b667080358bbbd444693b20180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81eec1f6ee4405401ff40539cf37d1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f6aac9b4d8e9449b9eed627c3cd47ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78eb47370c28394e2312174786e0f715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c19301d113ec019bab895c6c2e358ef</data>
      <data key="d3">157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANTEIRO DE OBRAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">The "CANTEIRO DE OBRAS" (construction site) is the designated location where construction activities are executed and equipment is utilized. As a workplace, it must strictly adhere to safety standards, including the application of safety norms, the use of Personal Protective Equipment (EPIs), and compliance with the Occupational Risk Management Plan (PGR). The site is required to maintain specific infrastructure, such as medical assistance facilities and designated areas where workers must remain after decompression procedures. Additionally, the "CANTEIRO DE OBRAS" must implement fire prevention measures and ensure that emergency exits are clearly signaled. To ensure regulatory compliance and operational safety, all required technical and maintenance documents, as well as safety documentation, must be readily available on-site, and all installations must follow applicable installation norms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e4f962ddfced8cca5c2aff7369a661b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1cac7a88894996eee964f97e7f53b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-589cdcf81c05ee920949a7fd05f6584a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e39a70a36c8f0f96a14271e365cd6351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40efae49bf166a100a9e409886cf4395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27bda215a442c90cb021c21b98db115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861e9f7632d4dfd81c4b7f8a9c0fdea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea78fb35e1fd216f5630ffebbc33a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f7df212717dd8ee2d97d84f42a97ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcad9f8ab5b70f8cb31dc94989c157e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780e0f65c9bb24868086ccd3f8d592e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-461b0578830e92eea6081cabfa2c7404</data>
      <data key="d3">159</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINISTÉRIO DO TRABALHO E EMPREGO (MTE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ministério do Trabalho e Emprego (MTE) is a Brazilian government body responsible for labor regulation and the issuance of normative decrees, including multiple orders for updates across various years such as 2013, 2024, 2025, and 2026. The MTE has issued several significant portarias (orders), most notably Portaria nº 1.897/2013, which altered work safety norms, and Portaria nº 598 of 2004, which updated the NR-10 standard. Additionally, the ministry is the issuing authority for Portaria nº 592 regarding fixation devices and other normative orders cited in relevant texts. Collectively, these actions underscore the MTE's central role in governing labor standards and safety regulations in Brazil.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9db29ce757dabf3f7cfeb504155acd7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81eec1f6ee4405401ff40539cf37d1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0493e5a610c1e30af5c60f7524c9e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea22aefdc64a322b6e5679d34d0f8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5936a71a74343d6130e3c767256974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc9d148efe9a2559b7beaa15d4eb102</data>
      <data key="d3">162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FABRICANTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">The FABRICANTE is the company responsible for producing various equipment, including cranes (gruas), scaffolding, anchoring devices, and other industrial apparatuses. As the manufacturer, the FABRICANTE holds several key responsibilities: it must provide the original operation manual and instruction manuals, with specific obligations to ensure that instructions for scaffolding are available in Portuguese. The entity's official identification details, specifically its legal name (razão social) and tax registration number (CNPJ), are required to be included in load plans and associated documentation. Furthermore, the FABRICANTE may specify the periodicity for certification and maintenance; the absence of such identification or defined maintenance schedules can necessitate the generation of specific technical reports (laudos). Finally, all operational procedures, recommendations, and checklists issued by the FABRICANTE must be strictly followed to ensure proper equipment usage and safety compliance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a87a3f81bc41b911db4b5e5d5f0dcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc556663e5d61db34218f36477303b44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f147b6a0c9b5cced56b4f6a670faf21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-749c2d920844c1bc2154c445fae4f3a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea78fb35e1fd216f5630ffebbc33a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de72701d9a6338255c6594fcfabb4d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28f3dbec47aed130afea6282dbc514ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c19301d113ec019bab895c6c2e358ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d76a42d252722ee5987d1c03002e78b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a4297618074b93c8abbfea3ab8bc40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7be1a396d630b24f28daad35f3ca0c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc56add9155f3804c44e96aaffd8d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38329ca5bd7388723ab2479ab41baab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9507a58112032a1366818361a0ca02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ef538556a551b7484cd4f959f104da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ba30f0a53c36f36a6dd512887c3a223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78eb47370c28394e2312174786e0f715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cf6f4889c3248de07b4fa8be118ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f7df212717dd8ee2d97d84f42a97ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81eec1f6ee4405401ff40539cf37d1e6</data>
      <data key="d3">182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROFISSIONAL LEGALMENTE HABILITADO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">A "PROFISSIONAL LEGALMENTE HABILITADO" é um especialista legalmente qualificado e autorizado por lei para atuar em diversas áreas técnicas e de segurança, garantindo a conformidade com normas regulamentares. As responsabilidades deste profissional abrangem a elaboração de projetos, laudos e planos de segurança em obras, bem como a aprovação da concentração de cargas em pontos específicos de telhados ou coberturas. Adicionalmente, a PROFISSIONAL LEGALMENTE HABILITADO está habilitada a projetar, autorizar e liberar escavações, além de ser responsável pelo projeto de equipamentos específicos, como serras circulares. No âmbito da gestão operacional e de segurança, este especialista supervisiona treinamentos, elabora projetos de sistemas de teste e monitora operações excepcionais, tais como o transporte de pessoas ou a instalação de placas. Por fim, a PROFISSIONAL LEGALMENTE HABILITADO possui a autoridade legal para modificar medidas de segurança, desde que tais alterações mantenham o nível de segurança original estabelecido.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-58fd45d2ee14671afd511b654fd72573&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a87a3f81bc41b911db4b5e5d5f0dcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc556663e5d61db34218f36477303b44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1afdc59c2d3726d04360a596f2f00fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f3fe8f8bfb9a820642da6555684412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df2326a15cc9705c8dbcd431d7762be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea78fb35e1fd216f5630ffebbc33a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c6e460c3d4f5d08be83abfcf6670e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcad9f8ab5b70f8cb31dc94989c157e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c698fd9dbd4746b8c175f22d62ca2788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f6aac9b4d8e9449b9eed627c3cd47ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1cac7a88894996eee964f97e7f53b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb1e0c16652291b0fd4eb8fdca5edb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777529d0ca6ad0353d174f0c0945acab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de72701d9a6338255c6594fcfabb4d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73989acf24197e9db670e73a0b363e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8256f00c2800357558f3e2c0d46b5d01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27bda215a442c90cb021c21b98db115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbf99e538c6200c878721962d99f90a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c19301d113ec019bab895c6c2e358ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20876814c61294bf395d2f121a24bddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75a6634b9377c3127262a76a0c6068e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55d1bf9243ba1aec47c5b4073afe46ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9507a58112032a1366818361a0ca02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ef538556a551b7484cd4f959f104da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff7ee508bd72306907acf96114dabee0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f780e0f65c9bb24868086ccd3f8d592e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fcca385fcdfc2bf69eb2e54c234a970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ba30f0a53c36f36a6dd512887c3a223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ef69391dd4e50ae486de13fe53bc42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-020c713238c5b6f009cdf20567f7c222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cf6f4889c3248de07b4fa8be118ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8035da2289e8087164d9a280d2a5d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8cfec1e4a84598830f42efa05e35e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8335d33c4efb992b42a42fa3597b5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f7df212717dd8ee2d97d84f42a97ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f32ce9b667080358bbbd444693b20180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81eec1f6ee4405401ff40539cf37d1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3502cb66477505db0e22df45c318467</data>
